{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/main/schema/mbmap-2.schema.json",
  "mbmap": 2,
  "vendor": "Growatt",
  "model": "Inverters, 3000 register range",
  "models": ["MIN", "MIC", "MOD", "TL-X", "TL-XH", "MOD TL3-XH"],
  "vendor_website": "growatt.com",
  "description": "Single- and three-phase string inverters (TL-X, TL-XH, MOD TL3-XH) that use the 3000-range input registers of the Growatt protocol",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-14",
  "source": "Growatt Inverter Modbus RTU Protocol V1.24",
  "sources": [
    {"title": "Growatt Inverter Modbus RTU Protocol", "version": "V1.24", "url": "https://github.com/johanmeijer/grott/raw/master/documentatie/Growatt-Inverter-Modbus-RTU-Protocol-II-V1-24-English-new.pdf", "note": "input registers 3000-3124 and holding registers 3000-3016 (section \"Use for TL-X and TL-XH\"), plus a few holding registers of the first group; linked in issue #186"}
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Difference from the TL3-X / MAX / MIX / SPH map: that map reads the first register group (input 0-124). This one reads the 3000-3124 group, which TL-X / TL-XH (MIN) and MOD TL3-XH inverters use for live data; the same quantities sit at different addresses (for example output power at 3023-3024 instead of 35-36) and the status register is split into a mode byte and a state byte.",
    "The document lists MIN as TL-X / TL-XH / TL-XH US. It does not name MIC or MOD models separately, except MOD TL3-XH, which it gives the same 3000-3124 input range; MIC is assumed to belong to the same family.",
    "Only the 3000-3124 input group is mapped. The document also describes 3125-3374 (storage and battery data of the TL-XH variants); those registers are not mapped here.",
    "32-bit values are sent high word first. Registers the document leaves without a unit or marks reserved (PV4 values, reactive power, the DCI and GFCI currents) are left out.",
    "Meter-related registers (3041-3046, 3067-3078) only carry data when the inverter has a meter or CT connected.",
    "Holding registers 0-124 follow the first group; only a few common ones are repeated here. The 03 range for these inverters is 0-124 and 3000-3124.",
    "Default serial settings follow the first-group map: 9600 baud, 8N1, address range 1-254. The document for this group does not state them again.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "unit_id": 1,
  "baudrate": 9600,
  "parity": "N",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "max_read_registers": 125,
  "x_status": "official",
